      "TWA\nE LINDBERGH LINE\nFASTEST\nSHORTEST\nCOAST to COAST\nTRANSCONTINENTAL\n\u0026 WESTERN\nU2. INC.\nEFFECTIVE JULY 1st, 1936",
      "LEAVE\nNEW YORK\n5:00 P.M.\nor 7:00 P.M.\nOVERNIGHT\nSlicing diagonally across America on the short-\ncut \"Lindbergh Route\" from coast to coast-flying\n200-miles-an-hour\nDouglas Luxury\nSkyliners\nTWA provides unequalled speed\n- overnight or\ndaylight — between the East and major Pacific\nCoast cities.\nAnd - Easterners may visit both Los Angeles\nand San\nFrancisco at no\nextra\nfare.\nWesterners may visit both\nNew York and Washington at no\nextra fare. Ask also about TWA's\n\"optional\"\nand\n\"circle\"\nroutings\nto any point in America.\nARRIVE\nLOS ANGELES\n8:00 A.M.\nor 9:27 A.M.\nGREAT FALLC\nCACRAMENTO\nAN FRANCICCO\nLOS ANGELES\nBOULDER DAM\nGRAND CANYON\nWINSLOW\nBOU CHICAGO\nKANSAS CITY\nCALANANA COINC\nWICHITA\n-ST. LOUIS\nATLANTIC OCEANE\nGULF OF MEXICO\nTWA System\n= Connecting Lines\nmOther Lines\nTWA IS THE COOL WAY FOR SUMMER TRAVEL\nAlr conditionina units pre-cool\nTWA\ncabins before and\nbe-\nBeat the heat! Fly TWA\nOur special\nair conditioning units at all major air-\nports pump fresh, de-humidified, chilled\nair into TWA planes before and be-\ntween each flight.\nThe insulated cab-\nins retain this coolness while the plane\nclimbs to the cool upper air\nwhere\nnatural coolness prevails even on the\nhottest days.\nHere the plane's auto-\nmatic ventilation system takes over,\nkeeps the cabin supplied with clean,\ncool air in abundant volume.\nIndividual\nventilators suo\nplement the cabin ventila-\ntion\none\ncooling\nsystem.\nWESTBOUND\nREAD DOWN\nCOMPLETE SCHEDULES-COAST TO COAST\nEASTBOUND\nREAD UP\n2nd Sky\n3rd Sky\nFlight Fit. 21-1 Flight 11 Flt. 15-9 Fight 5 Chiet s\nFlight 19 Flig\n3:50PM\n-Y SCHED\nILy Boston (ET) AA\nLv New York (Newark)\n7.2704\n6.220\n7:57PM\n5:55PM\n9:54PM\n7:55PM\nNON-\nSTOP\n2:37PM\n3 :35PMO\n845AM 12:40PM\n2.280\n3:00PM • 5:15PM •0\nbus (CT)\n(CT)\n8:00AM\n8.00AM\nr Los Angeles ® (Burbank A\nBoth 16 does to Monday saturdara\nNO OTHER TRANSCONTINENTAL AIRLINE FLIES OVER EITHER GRAND CANYON\nOR BOULDER DAM. TWA SHOWS YOU BOTH."
